    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the structure already established in this class. The preceding method (the `\"SILVER\"`/`\"BRONZE\"` loyalty-tier derivation) shows `Owner` already hosts small `@Transient` computed getters derived from the owner's own fields, so `getLocality()` lands in the right unit and reads as a natural sibling rather than a foreign concern.\n\n- The lookup table is a `private static final Map.of(...)` constant co-located with its single consumer, which keeps the fixed data next to the one method that reads it. Placing the static field mid-class (rather than at the top with other fields) is a minor convention deviation, but the locality-of-reference payoff is a defensible tradeoff and not worth churning.\n- No duplication: the city\u2192region mapping exists in exactly one place; the Javadoc and the OpenAPI `description` restate it in prose but that's documentation, not logic.\n- The method is a single-responsibility one-liner (`getOrDefault(this.city, \"UNKNOWN\")`) \u2014 the UNKNOWN fallback is expressed declaratively rather than branching, which is idiomatic.\n- The OpenAPI addition mirrors the adjacent derived `readOnly` field (the loyalty string) exactly in shape and placement, so the schema change is consistent with its neighbors.\n\n`Owner` is not becoming a catch-all \u2014 it's accruing a second small derived accessor in an area that already holds one, which a maintainer here would find natural.",
